==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*walaz}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*welh₃-|t=to hit, to strike}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|wal}}, {{cog|goh|wal}}, and {{cog|non|valr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|wæl}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|n}}

# [[slaughter]], [[carnage]]
# the [[slain]]
#* [https://archive.org/details/anglosaxonchroni01thor/page/110/mode/1up The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle]
#*: {{quote|ang|''<small>An. DCCCXXIII</small> Hēr wæs Wāla ġefeoht ⁊ Defna æt Gafulforda. ⁊ þȳ ilcan ġēare ġefeaht Eċġbryht cyning ⁊ Beornwulf cyning on Ellendūne, ⁊ Eċġbryht siġe nam, ⁊ þǣr wæs myċel wæl ġeslæġen.''|<small>Year 823</small> In this year there was a battle between the Welsh and the Devons at Gafulford. And in the same year Kings Edgebright and Beornwulf fought at Allington, and Edgebright took the victory, and many were slain there.}}
